38,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
39,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings suggest a vulnerability in our dependencies. While local halls are resilient, our external contractors prioritize larger clients, meaning our timelines could slip based on factors entirely outside our control. We must be cautious of such volatility.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh no, that's so sad! I found out that people in the outer wards lost their bus links, so it's really hard for them to reach us. Also, people are using the catalogue late at night, but we're already closed!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings reveal a concerning pattern in our funding. The county grant only covers session fees for the first year, leaving the operating budget to absorb them thereafter. Furthermore, we are overrunning vehicle costs while returning equipment funds.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,May,,"It's funny how we always talk about ""new"" ideas, but the records show we've already had wins! Former outreach stops in outer wards actually beat our midweek main building numbers. We just need to stop ignoring the past.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found that we have some retired tradespeople helping us, but... nobody on the payroll is actually trained to supervise them. Also, the person who certified our power tools retired in the spring.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, your findings on supervision and certification are concerning. When combined with my discovery regarding contractor volatility, it appears we are operating on a fragile foundation. We cannot afford a plan that relies on external schedules or uncertified staff.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, you're right, it sounds a bit scary! But @May, your news is so wonderful! If outreach was that popular, maybe we can bring the library to the people who can't reach us anymore because of the buses!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, while outreach is a noble goal, we must be cautious. My findings suggest that if we start new sessions via grants, the cost will fall on our operating budget after a year, which is already strained by vehicle overruns.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're always so worried about the budget! But why fund something ""new"" and risky when we know outreach actually works? The data is right there; we just have to be brave enough to use it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think George is right to be worried. If we start something new, the staff will have to handle it... and I'm worried we don't have the right training or people to actually manage it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, bravery is not a substitute for stability. If we implement a plan that depends on contractors who prioritize others or staff we cannot legally supervise, the project will fail regardless of past popularity. We need a predictable model.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I understand being careful, but we can't just leave the people in the outer wards behind! If they can't get to us, the library isn't really for everyone, right? We have to find a way!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I do not wish to leave anyone behind, but we must be realistic. If we expand outreach without a sustainable funding structure, we risk a service that collapses in its second year. We need a plan that is financially viable long-term.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, ""financially viable"" shouldn't just mean ""cheap."" It means investing in what actually draws a crowd! If we keep playing it safe, we're just managing a decline. Let's look for a win we've already proven.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just don't want the staff to be overwhelmed. If we pick a project that needs special skills we don't have on the roster, it'll just be more pressure on everyone... and that's not fair.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"It is clear we are all identifying different points of failure. Whether it is financial instability, lack of supervision, or contractor volatility, the common thread is a lack of control. We must prioritize a proposal that is self-sufficient and predictable.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I totally agree that we need a plan that works, but we can't forget the people! If we pick something that doesn't help those who can't reach us, we're missing the point of a library! Let's find a way!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,George,,"I agree that the people are the priority, but a service that vanishes after twelve months is not a service at all. We must find a proposal that avoids the trap of short-term grant funding.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,May,,"You're all so focused on the ""what if"" that you're missing the ""what was."" We have a proven track record of success with outreach and community groups. Let's stop overthinking and pick a winner!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope we can find something that doesn't put too much pressure on the staff. I'm just worried that we're forgetting about the people who have to actually do the work every day.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
