62,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
63,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Looking at the options, the Digital Archive Portal seems the most stable. It avoids the contractor volatility of scanning if we use internal tools, and unlike the Mobile Branch, it doesn't depend on road conditions or vehicle budgets.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I see your point, but the Mobile Branch Service is just perfect! It solves the bus problem for the outer wards and brings the library to the people who can't reach us! It's so exciting!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the Mobile Branch is an appealing idea, but it is a financial trap. My findings show our vehicle costs already overrun, and the grant would only cover the first year, leaving us stranded in the second.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, you're still stuck on the numbers! The Mobile Branch is exactly what the records told us works. Outreach in the outer wards was a hit; why ignore a proven winner just because you're afraid of a budget line?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I'm really worried about the Maker Workshop. I found out we don't have anyone to certify the power tools anymore, and no one on staff is trained to supervise the facilitators. It seems too risky for the staff.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, your concern regarding the Maker Workshop is a critical point of failure. Similarly, the Mobile Branch is too dependent on volatile vehicle budgets and road conditions. We must avoid any plan that relies on factors we cannot control.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I understand, but the Digital Archive doesn't help the people who can't get to a computer or a branch! If we want to be a library for everyone, we have to be brave and help the outer wards!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, bravery without a plan is merely recklessness. The Digital Archive is a sustainable resource. Unlike the Mobile Branch, it does not risk a total collapse once the initial grant expires and the vehicle costs mount.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, you call it recklessness, but I call it listening to the data! The Digital Archive is just a fancy way of repeating the digitisation failure from six years ago. Why gamble on a portal when we know people actually show up for outreach?","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think the Language Learning Circles might be better. They use partner organizations and trained facilitators, so maybe the staff won't have to do everything themselves? It seems less stressful than the other options.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the Language Learning Circles are a reasonable alternative, as they shift the operational burden to partners. However, the Digital Archive remains the most predictable, provided we avoid the contractor pitfalls I identified. It is the least volatile choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I like the Language Learning Circles too! But @George, if we can't do the Mobile Branch, maybe the Circles can happen in the outer wards? We have to find a way to reach those people!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, if the Circles are coordinated through partner organizations, they may be more sustainable. However, we must ensure the funding for these facilitators doesn't simply vanish after the first year, leaving us with an unfunded mandate.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,May,,"@George, you're obsessing over the first year again! Look at the records: the partner-run groups from six years ago are still meeting unaided. That's the definition of sustainable. The Circles are a proven, low-cost win!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think May is right about the partner groups. If the partners handle the training and the teaching, the staff won't have to absorb all the work. It feels like the safest choice for everyone's well-being.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The evidence suggests that the Language Learning Circles are the most pragmatic choice. They avoid the contractor volatility of the Archive, the financial and road risks of the Mobile Branch, and the safety liabilities of the Workshop. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm a little sad we can't do the Mobile Branch, but the Language Learning Circles sound wonderful! If they happen in the community, we can still reach the people in the outer wards. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,George,,"I have listened to your points. While I remain cautious about the funding structure, the use of partner organizations makes the Language Learning Circles the most sustainable and least risky option. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,May,,"Finally! It took a while, but you all caught up to the data. The Circles are a proven winner that doesn't break the bank or the staff. I'm happy to vote for Option A!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we all agree. It feels like the Language Learning Circles are the only option that doesn't put too much pressure on the staff. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
